WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:09.770
X sixteen is the Second Isodynamic Point of triangle A B C: the second common intersection of the three Apollonian circles, lying outside the circumcircle on the Brocard axis.

2
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:23.013
Its trilinear coordinates are sine of A minus pi over three, to sine of B minus pi over three, to sine of C minus pi over three, and like X fifteen, its pedal triangle with respect to A B C is strictly equilateral.

3
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:32.240
On the central lines layer, X sixteen lies on the Brocard axis through X three, X six, and X fifteen, and on lines X two X thirteen and X four X eighteen.

4
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:42.700
X sixteen is the isogonal conjugate of the Second Isogonic Center X fourteen, and the inverse of the First Isodynamic Point X fifteen in the circumcircle of triangle A B C.
